# Instruction guards from thread-index predicates over the CTA's 64
# threads: a load under `%tid.x == 0 and %tid.x < 32` runs on lane 0 of
# warp 0. The branch on the and.pred selects the fallthrough block for
# the other 63, lanes 1-31 of warp 0 and warp 1, which run its 8-byte
# store 63 times, and the guard on a loaded value keeps that store's
# count and the CTA's store bytes bounds. That value, loaded at an
# address the lanes of a warp read alike, is one for the warp: a warp
# stores on all its lanes or on none, so a request's sectors are exact.
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/guards.ptx | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_guards( // block 64×1×1 | per CTA: global load 516 B, store <= 1,734 B; param load 1,024 B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	ld.global.f32 	%f1, [%rd6]; // global load [4·%tid.x + param_0] sectors/req 4–5 (ideal 4){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	@%p3 ld.global.f32 	%f2, [%rd6+512]; // warp 0 × lane 0 | exec 1/CTA | global load [4·%tid.x + param_0 + 512] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	@%p6 st.global.u32 	[%rd4+40], %r2; // exec <= 64/CTA | global store [param_1 + 40] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.b64 	[%rd4+48], %rd5; // [<block 1>] warp 0 × lane 1-31 ∪ warp 1 × lane * | exec 63/CTA | global store [param_1 + 48] sectors/req 1 (ideal 1){{$}}
